## Command

```shell
biome inspect plugins
```

## `biome.json`

```json
{
  "plugins": [
    { "path": "./unfiltered.grit", "includes": ["src/**/*.ts"] },
    "./unfiltered.grit",
    { "path": "./filtered.grit", "includes": ["src/**/*.ts", "!**/*.test.ts"] },
    { "path": "./throw.ts", "includes": ["src/**/*.ts"] },
    "./broken"
  ],
  "overrides": [
    {
      "includes": ["tests/**"],
      "plugins": [
        { "path": "./filtered.grit", "includes": ["**/*.test.ts"] },
        { "path": "./throw.ts", "includes": ["**/*.test.ts"] },
        { "path": "./unfiltered.grit", "includes": ["**/*.test.ts"] }
      ]
    },
    { "includes": ["scripts/**"], "plugins": ["./filtered.grit"] }
  ]
}
```

## `broken/biome-manifest.json`

```json
{ "version": 2 }
```

## `filtered.grit`

```grit
`console.log($message)`
```

## `throw.ts`

```ts
throw new Error('must not execute');
```

## `unfiltered.grit`

```grit
`console.log($message)`
```

# Termination Message

```block
configuration ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  × 1 plugin in the configuration has an error.
  
  The configuration enables 2 plugin rules and 1 JavaScript plugin.
  
  Local plugins
  
  - unfiltered.grit (rule name: unfiltered)
  
  Rules that apply only to matching files
  
  - filtered.grit (rule name: filtered), for files matching any of:
    - includes: [src/**/*.ts, !**/*.test.ts]
    - override includes: [tests/**] and includes: [**/*.test.ts]
    - override includes: [scripts/**]
  
  JavaScript plugins
  
  - throw.ts, for files matching any of:
    - includes: [src/**/*.ts]
    - override includes: [tests/**] and includes: [**/*.test.ts]
  
  i Biome doesn't run JavaScript plugins during inspection, so their rule names aren't listed.
  
  Plugins with errors
  
  broken
  
  × The Biome manifest broken/biome-manifest.json is invalid.
  
  × Unsupported version 2.
  
  i Biome manifests must use version 1.
  


```
